On Thu, 9 Mar 2005 wolverinefan@gmail.com wrote:

> The 2nd entry in the Early Strategy Series for Newbies.  How do you
> handle sinks in general?  Do you pass them up early on or kick/quaff
> them?  Drop rings down them?  At what point do you do this?

As puddings and foocubi are quite hard to beat in the early game and sinks
don't give lots of potential goodies (except a few unided rings or
identification of a random -potentially harmfull- potion), I avoid them in
the early game.

If I have 2 copies of the same ring, or a single cursed copy (found
cursed, so potentially harmfull), I drop the ring to identify it (usefull
for 2 copies, quite useful alos for some cursed rings (especially
negatively enchanted rings of gain/increase something)). Of course, I
start by price-iding rings, so I won't loose a ring of polymorph that way
(may found a ring of polycontrol later and that makes things great... plus
uncursing a ring is not too hard even early).

Later, when I can kill pudding (or strat farming if I intended to) and
pratice (almost) safe sex, kick, kick and wake that foocubi. Gaining a
level really worth the try.

